{
  "schema": "trueopen-rest-json-shapes-v1",
  "contract": "Node REST gateway JSON rendering",
  "notes": [
    "Bodies are rendered by the Node REST gateway: the Cosmos API server gateway marshaler (gogoproto JSONPb with OrigName and EmitDefaults) followed by the Node response encoder that applies shared.v1.rest_bytes_encoding. They are shapes, not chain data: populated bodies use placeholders (string \"s\", integer 1, the first declared non-zero enum value, and 32 bytes of ab for every bytes field).",
    "Field names are the proto field names (snake_case), never lowerCamelCase. Every field is emitted, including zero values, except an absent Hash32 (see below).",
    "bytes: a field annotated REST_BYTES_ENCODING_HASH32_LOWER_HEX is 64 lowercase hex characters with no 0x prefix; an unset one is omitted from the object. A field annotated REST_BYTES_ENCODING_PROTOJSON_BASE64 is standard padded Base64; an unset one is \"\".",
    "Integers: int64, uint64 and fixed64 fields are JSON strings of decimal digits; int32 and uint32 fields are JSON numbers. shared.v1.Amount.atomic_units is a string field and so is always a string.",
    "Enums are their full value names (for example TASK_TYPE_CHAT). An unset message field is null. A oneof renders only its set member (active or terminal for QueryTask).",
    "A value that uses repeated message fields renders one placeholder element in populated bodies."
  ],
